<?php
/**
 * Hub Market — the seller dashboard's charts draw again.
 *
 * CL036-DEV01.32 item 4. A copy of
 * Vnecoms_VendorsDashboard::dashboard.phtml with FOUR characters changed, kept
 * as a theme override so composer can still update the module.
 *
 * THE CHARTS WERE NOT A STYLING PROBLEM. The three tabs (Orders, Amounts,
 * Credits) were blank because the page threw:
 *
 *     Uncaught TypeError: $(...).size is not a function
 *         at drawTransactionChart (dashboard:1654)
 *
 * `.size()` was deprecated in jQuery 1.8 and REMOVED in 3.0; this install
 * ships jQuery 3.7.1. The module still calls `$(data).size()` in all three
 * draw functions, so the first one throws.
 *
 * ALL THREE TABS DIE ON THE FIRST THROW, not just Credits: the three draws run
 * one after another inside the same `.done()` callback, so the exception in
 * drawTransactionChart means drawOrdersChart and drawAmountsChart are never
 * reached. That is why the whole graph panel was empty rather than one tab.
 *
 * `$(data).length` is the exact replacement -- `.size()` was only ever a method
 * wrapper around `.length` -- so the "No Data Found" branch still behaves the
 * same when a period genuinely has no rows.
 *
 * SECOND, SEPARATE BUG FIXED HERE: drawAmountsChart's no-data branch wrote its
 * message into `#orders-chart`. A copy-paste slip in the module -- it would
 * have printed "No Data Found" into the Orders tab while the Amounts tab
 * stayed blank, which is a confusing thing to leave behind once the charts
 * start drawing at all.
 *
 * Nothing else is changed. Re-diff against the module's own copy after any
 * Vnecoms upgrade.
 */
